  <section class="cs-section" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
    <p class="bb-eyebrow">01 / THE PROBLEM TO SOLVE</p>
    <div><h2 id="problem-title">The bill is only<br><em>part of the job.</em></h2>
    <p>A salon billing workflow involves more than entering a total. The application needs to connect selected services, customer details, membership eligibility, payment methods, and the staff delivering those services.</p>
    <p>I designed Newbilling around that connected workflow, with a service catalogue feeding into bills and saved transactions feeding into reports.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="cs-section" aria-labelledby="solution-title">
    <p class="bb-eyebrow">02 / WHAT I BUILT</p>
    <div><h2 id="solution-title">One workspace.<br><em>Connected details.</em></h2>
      <div class="cs-features">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Billing & receipts</h3><p>Select services, apply flat or percentage discounts, record cash, UPI, or card payments, revisit saved bills, and print receipts.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Customers & memberships</h3><p>Manage walk-in customers and members, look up customer details, track membership renewals, and apply eligible membership offers.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Services & staff</h3><p>Maintain service prices and availability, manage staff records, and connect staff assignments to the billing workflow.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Business reports</h3><p>Review daily, weekly, monthly, or yearly activity, including service sales, membership renewals, payment breakdowns, taxes, and discounts.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="cs-section" aria-labelledby="decisions-title">
    <p class="bb-eyebrow">03 / INSIDE THE BUILD</p>
    <div><h2 id="decisions-title">Useful interfaces.<br><em>Careful business logic.</em></h2>
      <h3>Keep calculations on the server</h3><p>Rails validates service items, quantities, customer ownership, discounts, and membership eligibility before saving a bill. The interface helps enter the data; the server checks the business rules.</p>
      <h3>Preserve the details of saved bills</h3><p>Bill items retain service names and prices so a later catalogue price change does not silently rewrite the original transaction.</p>
      <h3>Connect reports to saved transactions</h3><p>Reports combine bills and membership renewals for the selected period, using the Asia/Kolkata time zone to group activity.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="cs-section" aria-labelledby="result-title">
    <p class="bb-eyebrow">04 / THE RESULT</p>
    <div><h2 id="result-title">From service selection<br><em>to the daily picture.</em></h2>
      <p>The finished application connects billing, customer records, memberships, staff, and reporting behind a signed-in workspace. This case study describes the implemented features; customer adoption and time-saving metrics have not been measured.</p>
